1
00:00:01,960 --> 00:00:04,901
Narancia, when you get a
sec, let me see that key.

2
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:10,329
Look for the turtle at the water
fountain, and use this key.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,760
Did you really...?

4
00:00:15,860 --> 00:00:17,520
The thankful death!

5
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:20,121
Just the driver.

6
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:21,860
Everyone else is gone.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:27,830
Yes!

8
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:29,961
It looks like they took the bait!

9
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:34,249
How'd this frickin'
hook get under my skin?

10
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:37,815
This can't be the guy that's
trying to age us to death!

11
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:06,630
Thank you.

12
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:43,537
Thank

13
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:44,937
you

14
00:01:45,020 --> 00:01:52,020
so

15
00:01:55,780 --> 00:01:57,020
much for watching.

16
00:01:58,060 --> 00:01:59,260
Temasita, Junior!

17
00:02:04,220 --> 00:02:05,340
Fighting God!

18
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:12,620
Yo, big bro!

19
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:13,960
Where are you?

20
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:15,800
Come on, cut it out!

21
00:02:16,060 --> 00:02:18,997
I know Bucciarati and his
goons are on the train, but...

22
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:21,620
Who the hell is tugging on my hook?

23
00:02:21,860 --> 00:02:24,000
No way it could be that girl Trish!

24
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:27,020
No teenage girl has that much power.

25
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:31,476
Well, whoever they are, they're a
human being that weighs 68 kilograms.

26
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:33,660
Time to reel this sucker in.

27
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:38,054
What's with this hook?

28
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:39,620
It's getting deeper.

29
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:42,193
Could this be the enemy's stand ability?

30
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:44,240
It's so quick.

31
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:46,929
It's chewing up my arm
like a damn missile.

32
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,680
I can't break the line.

33
00:02:54,440 --> 00:02:56,322
Ooh, looks like I snagged Mista.

34
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:59,020
I definitely felt a bullet hit my line.

35
00:02:59,420 --> 00:03:02,180
And the asshole with
the gun is Guido Mista.

36
00:03:02,660 --> 00:03:06,520
Well played, Quick Draw, but
my line is indestructible.

37
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:10,180
Now where will the reverberation
from the bullet go?

38
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:13,016
Let's reel you in and give it a look.

39
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:16,054
I've gotta rip this thing out and fast.

40
00:03:18,440 --> 00:03:22,260
I gotta do something, this thing
is gonna furrow into my brain!

41
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:24,870
Get out!

42
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:28,580
You're on, six bullets!

43
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:30,660
Pull this damn hook out of me!

44
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:35,820
Look, he's not here taking us for a ride!

45
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:39,078
It has more pulled than the
three of us put together!

46
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:40,617
Damn, seriously?

47
00:03:40,700 --> 00:03:42,288
I guess I'm on my own here.

48
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:44,325
So it's time for some surgery!

49
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:45,930
Yeah!

50
00:03:46,420 --> 00:03:47,340
Count on us!

51
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:49,020
We gotta track it down!

52
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:52,280
Failure is not an option,
so keep your eyes peeled!

53
00:03:53,260 --> 00:03:54,090
Huh?

54
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:55,600
What was that?

55
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:58,000
Did Mista fire off his revolver?

56
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:00,929
Who the hell are you
even shooting at, huh?

57
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:04,337
What, you trying to take out
one of these poor passengers?

58
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:09,077
I get what you're trying to do, using your
bullets to ferret me out like a sniper.

59
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:10,984
Whatever, you're still screwed!

60
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:12,577
Hope you enjoyed your hearing,

61
00:04:12,660 --> 00:04:15,836
because my hook is headed
straight for your inner ear!

62
00:04:26,820 --> 00:04:27,650
Ah!

63
00:04:27,733 --> 00:04:28,857
What are you guys doing?

64
00:04:28,940 --> 00:04:33,528
You gotta aim closer or else we're never
gonna blast the ice out of this room!

65
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:35,837
It's just a little lure!

66
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:36,817
You're almost there!

67
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:38,135
Keep it moving, guys!

68
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:40,181
Blast that ice, the King of Khan!

69
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:42,873
The primary target is getting ahead now!

70
00:04:43,060 --> 00:04:44,100
Go, ragazzi!

71
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:45,595
Shatter it to pieces!

72
00:04:56,420 --> 00:04:58,320
What are you doing?

73
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:02,737
Of course he would be
trying to keep himself cool.

74
00:05:02,820 --> 00:05:04,820
Talk about having a one-trek mind.

75
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:06,960
Damn it! You idiot!

76
00:05:07,540 --> 00:05:08,877
Now you've gone and done it!

77
00:05:08,960 --> 00:05:11,784
Was this guy supposed to
be the Pasty Pineapple?

78
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:13,920
Is this weird looking doobard guy?

79
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:15,560
It's him!

80
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:18,417
He's the guy that was
controlling that freaky hook!

81
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:21,735
Look, that fishing rod looking
thing must be his stand!

82
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:27,160
If I don't get some ice, Fro's age
accelerator's gonna kill me too!

83
00:05:29,160 --> 00:05:32,680
Please, you have to help me! Get off!

84
00:05:32,940 --> 00:05:34,200
I'm serious, geyser!

85
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:35,657
Get your rotten meds off of me!

86
00:05:35,740 --> 00:05:40,260
I feel so heavy, and all I
want to do is take a good nap.

87
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:46,800
I ordered a big juicy snake, too, and now
I don't even have the energy to enjoy it!

88
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:48,700
Get the prick away, you freak!

89
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:51,900
We did it!

90
00:05:52,020 --> 00:05:53,120
His hand is toast!

91
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:55,145
Get me staying here right now!

92
00:05:55,340 --> 00:05:56,620
Mista, you're clear!

93
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:02,080
Hey, Mista, come on!

94
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,144
The stand user's ready for you!

95
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:25,217
Alright now, six bullets.

96
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:28,006
Time for you all to get
back to your stations.

97
00:06:39,700 --> 00:06:42,060
I have one simple question for you.

98
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:46,877
You can ignore it if you want, but I'm
still going to ask, so just deal with it.

99
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:50,017
But I think there's something
you should know first.

100
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:54,806
If you can't find the words to muster up
a coherent response within two seconds,

101
00:06:55,060 --> 00:06:57,017
I'm going to shoot hot
lead into those beady

102
00:06:57,100 --> 00:06:59,512
targets framing that bugly nose of yours.

103
00:06:59,860 --> 00:07:01,420
It's uno, then due.

104
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:03,677
After that, it's bye-bye, pasty.

105
00:07:03,760 --> 00:07:06,700
If we're clear, I expect an honest answer.

106
00:07:07,640 --> 00:07:11,052
Where the hell is your
life-stealing companion hiding out?

107
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:13,310
Ooh, no.

108
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:15,060
I don't know, man.

109
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:17,037
I've been here wondering the same thing.

110
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:18,180
And do it.

111
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:19,340
Now die, Katsune.

112
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:23,040
Please, I need your help, sir.

113
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:27,280
Oh, juicy marbled steak
used to be my favorite meal.

114
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:28,657
Would you get out of the way?

115
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:31,597
You'll be chowing down on your
steak again before you know it.

116
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:33,580
No, I don't think I will.

117
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:38,760
Oh boy, instead I'll be bringing
about your demise. What?

118
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:40,155
Who the hell are you?

119
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:48,740
End his life, thankful death.

120
00:07:50,340 --> 00:07:51,170
What?

121
00:07:51,253 --> 00:07:52,083
How are you?

122
00:07:52,166 --> 00:07:54,697
Wait, you're not really an
old man at all, are you?

123
00:07:54,780 --> 00:07:56,720
You're a death geyser.

124
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:03,820
Death comes quicker using direct contact.

125
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:06,720
Once thankful death caresses you,

126
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:10,960
your body is filled with its
soul-sucking necrotic energy.

127
00:08:11,420 --> 00:08:13,500
My bullets are dying.

128
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:16,440
It's happening so fast.

129
00:08:17,020 --> 00:08:17,850
Shit.

130
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:27,477
Are you really my big bro
under that saggy skin?

131
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:31,857
Whoa that's so crazy you
had me completely fooled!

132
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:36,437
You were really something bro
man attacking your own body in

133
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:40,461
order to blend in with the of the
other passengers takes real guts.

134
00:08:45,340 --> 00:08:46,340
It is you!

135
00:08:46,540 --> 00:08:48,364
I mean, I knew it was, but wow!

136
00:08:48,560 --> 00:08:50,736
You never failed to impress, big bro.

137
00:08:55,140 --> 00:08:57,000
You absolute waste of space!

138
00:08:57,340 --> 00:09:00,399
What the hell was that
atrocious display back there?

139
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:03,657
How was I supposed to know the
guy was gonna shoot the ice?

140
00:09:03,740 --> 00:09:05,537
There was nothing I
could do, bro, I swear!

141
00:09:05,620 --> 00:09:07,057
You still don't get it, do you?

142
00:09:07,140 --> 00:09:08,960
You're a goddamn Mamoni!

143
00:09:09,240 --> 00:09:11,920
Not in the face, bro! Please! Have mercy!

144
00:09:13,680 --> 00:09:16,317
Pesci, do you want to
know why I'm pissed off?

145
00:09:16,400 --> 00:09:19,097
It's because you've been
cursed with such a weak spirit.

146
00:09:19,180 --> 00:09:23,277
The beanie-wearing bastard blasted
your ice, which threw you for a loop.

147
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:24,640
Fine, it happens.

148
00:09:25,160 --> 00:09:29,240
I'm also being aged, so this ain't
a walk in the park for me either.

149
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:32,897
That said, no one else from the team
would have stopped their attack.

150
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:35,257
Calling back your stand
at the moment of truth

151
00:09:35,340 --> 00:09:37,817
with the enemy is the very
definition of cowardice,

152
00:09:37,900 --> 00:09:38,730
little brother.

153
00:09:38,813 --> 00:09:41,877
No one else would have done so even
if they were being dismembered.

154
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:44,880
So like I said, you're a damn Mamoni.

155
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:48,037
You practically pissed yourself
in that battle with Nista.

156
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:49,767
And it wasn't about the ice.

157
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:53,357
Deep down in your heart of
hearts, terror took hold of you.

158
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:55,580
You need to man up now, Pesci.

159
00:09:56,160 --> 00:09:59,420
If you don't, glory will be
forever beyond our reach.

160
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:01,877
Bucciarati and his sidekicks will win.

161
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:04,257
If you don't want that
fate, then pay attention.

162
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:07,640
We're not the same as that
gang of ass-kissing losers.

163
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:11,177
We don't indulge in empty
threats or self-coddling

164
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:13,797
compliments to hide our
feeble shortcomings.

165
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:16,357
Our breed doesn't need
the aid of such low-brow

166
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:19,264
extravagances to enhance
our battle performance.

167
00:10:19,420 --> 00:10:22,660
For the moment, we visualize
the death of our enemy.

168
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:24,680
Their fate is sealed!

169
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:27,020
They cannot escape the inevitable!

170
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:40,740
Now then, let's be off,
Pesci, and have some ice.

171
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:45,677
I recall you saying there was another
soul hiding out in the driver's car,

172
00:10:45,760 --> 00:10:48,157
so let's hurry out there
and finish this mission.

173
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:50,817
I don't know what kind
of trick they're using,

174
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,841
but if that little harlot
is there, I'll find her.

175
00:11:09,400 --> 00:11:11,980
No, don't worry about Narancia.

176
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:15,960
That ice is for you.

177
00:11:16,220 --> 00:11:18,102
You're the one who must survive.

178
00:11:18,540 --> 00:11:20,620
Worry about your body temperature.

179
00:11:21,060 --> 00:11:25,257
It's going to take a lot more than a fan
and a damp towel to cool Narancia off.

180
00:11:25,340 --> 00:11:26,575
I know you know that.

181
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:30,014
The only thing that's going
to help him now is this ice.

182
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:33,141
At the rate he's aging,
he'll be the first to die.

183
00:11:33,620 --> 00:11:35,300
We're members of the Mafia.

184
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:38,541
We knew the dangers when
we accepted this mission.

185
00:11:38,940 --> 00:11:42,340
Know that your well-being
outweighs any of ours.

186
00:11:42,680 --> 00:11:44,151
Guarding you is our duty.

187
00:11:44,980 --> 00:11:48,156
Needless to say, you brought
none of this on yourself.

188
00:11:48,380 --> 00:11:49,600
You have my word.

189
00:11:49,860 --> 00:11:54,120
The culprit behind this attack will
meet their end by Meesta's hand.

190
00:11:54,420 --> 00:11:56,317
He'll find a way to pull through.

191
00:11:56,400 --> 00:11:57,440
I know it.

192
00:11:58,780 --> 00:11:59,610
Mista.

193
00:12:13,660 --> 00:12:15,980
They have to be in this car somewhere.

194
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:17,700
How are they hiding?

195
00:12:18,680 --> 00:12:19,510
Focus.

196
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:26,700
The key is to start thinking about
the world in four dimensions.

197
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:32,240
At the binario, Bucciarati picked up
a certain something sent by the boss.

198
00:12:33,260 --> 00:12:34,090
That's it.

199
00:12:34,173 --> 00:12:36,708
If I find that object,
I'll find our quarry.

200
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:39,280
Hey, Pesci.

201
00:12:40,040 --> 00:12:42,657
You felt another presence
in this car, right?

202
00:12:42,740 --> 00:12:45,677
Have you given any thought
to what it might have been?

203
00:12:45,760 --> 00:12:47,300
Can you still sense it?

204
00:12:48,080 --> 00:12:50,080
I told you everything I know, bro.

205
00:12:50,280 --> 00:12:51,339
It was just weird.

206
00:12:51,540 --> 00:12:54,617
I wish you wouldn't put so much
pressure on me all the time.

207
00:12:54,700 --> 00:12:56,477
I don't have the wits that you do.

208
00:12:56,560 --> 00:12:59,297
Pesci, Pesci, Pesci, Pesci untrue.

209
00:12:59,380 --> 00:13:02,520
I have unwavering faith in your ability,

210
00:13:02,900 --> 00:13:05,797
which is the reason I got
so angry with you earlier.

211
00:13:05,880 --> 00:13:07,420
You need self-confidence.

212
00:13:07,840 --> 00:13:11,017
If you can snap out of this
funk and come into your own,

213
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:14,577
I know you'll be the unbeatable
force of nature you were meant to be.

214
00:13:14,660 --> 00:13:15,601
What do you say?

215
00:13:15,940 --> 00:13:18,637
That feeling you had
is extremely important.

216
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:21,367
You need to focus on
unveiling what it meant.

217
00:13:21,460 --> 00:13:23,920
It's your time to shine at last, Pesci.

218
00:13:24,280 --> 00:13:26,300
You must have faith in yourself,

219
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:29,597
dear brother of mine, and
believe in your amazing power.

220
00:13:29,680 --> 00:13:30,680
I'm amazing?

221
00:13:30,980 --> 00:13:31,862
Yes, of course.

222
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:35,977
Now think hard and tell me anything
that comes to mind that might help us.

223
00:13:36,060 --> 00:13:38,317
Did something in
particular catch your eye?

224
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:41,920
Like some strange dark
object, for instance. Huh?

225
00:13:42,340 --> 00:13:43,560
A dark object?

226
00:13:44,300 --> 00:13:45,130
Oh, yeah.

227
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:46,980
I remember now, big bro.

228
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:50,497
I was about to look under this
seat here, but I got distracted.

229
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:52,880
I'm sure I saw something. Huh?

230
00:13:58,160 --> 00:13:59,957
Uh, wow, that's embarrassing.

231
00:14:00,040 --> 00:14:01,260
I guess I was wrong.

232
00:14:01,900 --> 00:14:03,460
I told you, Big Bro.

233
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:05,700
I knew my intuition was crap.

234
00:14:05,940 --> 00:14:06,877
Why can't I stop being useless?

235
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:09,097
Actually, I think you're on to something.

236
00:14:09,180 --> 00:14:10,010
Huh?

237
00:14:10,093 --> 00:14:11,037
Do you really mean it?

238
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:12,600
I'm proud of you, Pesci.

239
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:14,740
You just solved our mystery.

240
00:14:15,060 --> 00:14:18,178
There's now a light at the
end of this vexing tunnel.

241
00:14:18,280 --> 00:14:19,360
What do you mean?

242
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:20,697
What light did I find?

243
00:14:20,780 --> 00:14:25,662
Isn't it curious that there'd be random
animal feces under the seat of a train car?

244
00:14:26,640 --> 00:14:28,797
This shit didn't come from a rat.

245
00:14:28,880 --> 00:14:31,977
The thing would be long dead as
their lives are shorter lived than.

246
00:14:32,060 --> 00:14:36,617
Their stool whatever left this
excrement only did so a few moments ago.

247
00:14:36,700 --> 00:14:39,837
You starting to wonder
what all this means? Yeah.

248
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:44,117
Humans aren't the only species
capable of possessing a stand.

249
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:46,337
Which leaves only one explanation.

250
00:14:46,420 --> 00:14:49,237
We've got a unique animal
hiding in the shadows.

251
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:50,960
Mercy kill it. Thankful.

252
00:14:55,340 --> 00:14:56,170
Look!

253
00:14:56,253 --> 00:14:57,500
What the hell is that?

254
00:14:57,760 --> 00:14:59,500
Wait, it's a freaking turtle.

255
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:00,917
What's it doing here?

256
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,360
Concealing our prize.

257
00:15:02,540 --> 00:15:04,740
Trish, I can see the others, too.

258
00:15:05,040 --> 00:15:09,117
As expected, the boys are passing on
to the big nursing home in the sky.

259
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,380
It's time to strike.

260
00:15:10,720 --> 00:15:13,838
Hope you're ready for another
dose of my aging power.

261
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:15,280
Thankful death!

262
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:17,547
Hey, wait a second, big bro.

263
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:19,560
Look inside.

264
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:20,857
Aren't they supposed to die?

265
00:15:20,940 --> 00:15:24,257
to have another guy with them huh I think

266
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:26,869
one of their buddies
pulled a Houdini on us

267
00:15:45,780 --> 00:15:46,940
B-staff!

268
00:15:47,160 --> 00:15:48,680
You have to get up!

269
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:52,680
Here, take the last hunk of ice!

270
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:54,520
It'll make you all better!

271
00:15:56,300 --> 00:16:00,500
Maybe it happened because I'm always
expecting things to go sideways.

272
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:04,100
Or maybe I have my own
guardian angel out there.

273
00:16:04,620 --> 00:16:09,920
But storing ice in my hat was the best
decision I ever made. Number five,

274
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:12,797
I don't even want to think
about where I'd be right now if

275
00:16:12,880 --> 00:16:16,577
your razor-sharp instincts hadn't
turned back the hands of time.

276
00:16:16,660 --> 00:16:20,440
Your quick thinking totally
saved my ass, little buddy.

277
00:16:21,780 --> 00:16:27,420
The way you stopped the momentum of all
three of those bullets you should be proud.

278
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:33,597
Number five I have one
more favor to ask of you

279
00:16:33,680 --> 00:16:35,597
if you're about to say
one of us should go to.

280
00:16:35,680 --> 00:16:38,897
Number six has already
been revived and is on

281
00:16:38,980 --> 00:16:41,957
his way he's got the ice
from your pocket and he's

282
00:16:42,040 --> 00:16:43,977
Gonna tell everyone about
the two users who are

283
00:16:44,060 --> 00:16:46,957
closing in on the turtles
so you ain't gotta worry.

284
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:49,360
I couldn't ask for anything more.

285
00:16:49,680 --> 00:16:52,040
You should save that ice for the others.

286
00:16:52,460 --> 00:16:55,280
Don't think that I'll
be needing it anymore.

287
00:16:56,820 --> 00:16:58,840
Take care of everyone.

288
00:17:02,500 --> 00:17:05,177
I figured out which one
of them's missing, bro!

289
00:17:05,260 --> 00:17:06,240
It's Bucciarati!

290
00:17:06,460 --> 00:17:07,754
He's our missing goon!

291
00:17:08,340 --> 00:17:09,720
Forget Bucciarati!

292
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:12,217
All that matters is us
retrieving the girl.

293
00:17:12,300 --> 00:17:13,130
Alive!

294
00:17:13,213 --> 00:17:15,020
Get to work! Thankful death!

295
00:17:16,460 --> 00:17:18,080
He's attacking from above!

296
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:22,677
Your instincts are impressive, and I have
to say you're pretty light on your feet.

297
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:24,480
The man dressed in black.

298
00:17:25,220 --> 00:17:27,357
Once I off him, the others will recover.

299
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:28,793
You got it, Bucciarati!

300
00:17:29,080 --> 00:17:33,640
You get rid of this Soul bastard,
everyone will be as good as new! What?

301
00:17:33,780 --> 00:17:35,721
Why the hell is Mista stand here?

302
00:17:36,300 --> 00:17:39,697
I emptied my freakin' gun into
his skull at Point Blake Range!

303
00:17:39,780 --> 00:17:42,251
That should've been all she wrote for him!

304
00:17:42,500 --> 00:17:44,637
So how could that thing
have gotten ice in here?

305
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:47,073
Whatever you do, don't let it touch you!

306
00:17:47,220 --> 00:17:50,749
Direct contact with the stand
will make you age even faster!

307
00:17:52,920 --> 00:17:53,820
Get him!

308
00:18:05,020 --> 00:18:05,850
Shit!

309
00:18:05,980 --> 00:18:06,940
He's too quick!

310
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:11,820
Hey, brother!

311
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:13,597
Eyes on the prize!

312
00:18:13,680 --> 00:18:16,857
Focus on taking care of the
fools hiding in the turtle!

313
00:18:16,940 --> 00:18:18,657
Would you hurry up and do it?

314
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:20,858
Put these weevils out of commission!

315
00:18:31,060 --> 00:18:34,000
I admit you caught me
by surprise, Bucciarati.

316
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:38,798
To think that Miesta would go through
all that trouble to tip you off.

317
00:18:38,900 --> 00:18:42,577
Knocking off foes and protecting the
girl regardless of the human cost?

318
00:18:42,660 --> 00:18:45,425
That is the mission the
boss gave you, correct?

319
00:18:45,980 --> 00:18:47,800
You failed your Family.

320
00:18:48,600 --> 00:18:49,430
Die!

321
00:18:52,220 --> 00:18:53,240
The hell?

322
00:19:01,700 --> 00:19:03,800
I will fulfill my mission.

323
00:19:04,340 --> 00:19:06,100
And save my Family.

324
00:19:06,460 --> 00:19:09,460
If the only thing that's
standing in my way is you.

325
00:19:09,680 --> 00:19:12,260
Well then, victory's already well in hand.

326
00:19:13,480 --> 00:19:14,837
It's got speed.

327
00:19:14,920 --> 00:19:17,420
It's much faster than I was expecting.

328
00:19:18,900 --> 00:19:20,340
What did you call it?

329
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:22,836
Oh, yeah, Zipper Man, I think it was.

330
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,471
The name suits it nicely.

331
00:19:24,820 --> 00:19:29,057
There's no question that you are
naturally endowed with the gift of speed.

332
00:19:29,140 --> 00:19:31,357
But the sad fact of the matter is,

333
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:35,205
you still don't know the first
thing about using it, Bucciarati.

334
00:19:38,400 --> 00:19:42,940
I guess it's sort of obvious but
I'm a little short of breath.

335
00:19:45,880 --> 00:19:50,317
And from where I'm sitting the same
goes for you that tends to happen

336
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:55,657
you know when one uses their Stand at
full bore really how foolish of you

337
00:19:55,740 --> 00:19:59,497
clearly that hadn't entered your mind
when you Were ordering your zipper

338
00:19:59,580 --> 00:20:03,977
man to attack me at its maximum speed
and due to your lapse in judgment?

339
00:20:04,060 --> 00:20:06,160
and your rapid aging has resumed.

340
00:20:08,280 --> 00:20:11,897
Someone should have informed you of
this, but the greater the horsepower,

341
00:20:11,980 --> 00:20:13,274
the hotter the engine.

342
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:15,929
Us two are burning a
whole lot of calories.

343
00:20:16,180 --> 00:20:18,897
Since you seem to be a man
of moderate intelligence,

344
00:20:18,980 --> 00:20:20,597
I'm sure you can take my meaning.

345
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:24,445
What do you think is gonna happen
as your body heats up further?

346
00:20:27,280 --> 00:20:28,110
No!

347
00:20:28,680 --> 00:20:29,510
Uchirati!

348
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:31,270
Shit!

349
00:20:31,353 --> 00:20:32,817
The ice isn't working anymore.

350
00:20:32,900 --> 00:20:34,253
What am I gonna do now?

351
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:36,580
So, what's your next move, huh?

352
00:20:36,940 --> 00:20:39,740
The zipper you put on
me is starting to close.

353
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:42,097
Soon enough, I'll be right as rain.

354
00:20:42,180 --> 00:20:43,057
And look at that.

355
00:20:43,140 --> 00:20:45,077
There goes the one on my chin, too.

356
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:46,219
What's the matter?

357
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:48,892
You feeling a bit stiff and tuckered out?

358
00:20:50,980 --> 00:20:52,440
And this, Zipper Man!

359
00:20:53,520 --> 00:20:55,285
Really, you're so predictable.

360
00:20:55,400 --> 00:20:57,047
Take a dirt nap, Bucciarati!

361
00:20:59,520 --> 00:21:02,817
Once I'm done, you and your friends
will be off to the crematorium.

362
00:21:02,900 --> 00:21:05,757
But don't worry, we'll make sure
the girl is well taken care of.

363
00:21:05,840 --> 00:21:07,157
Would you stop talking?

364
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:09,828
I knew exactly what
would happen to my body.

365
00:21:09,920 --> 00:21:10,750
Huh?

366
00:21:10,833 --> 00:21:13,185
I was also well aware
that I could be captured.

367
00:21:13,340 --> 00:21:15,222
But a mission must be completed.

368
00:21:15,420 --> 00:21:16,980
And I'll protect my crew.

369
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:20,197
Kapos worth their salt
must be prepared for both.

370
00:21:20,280 --> 00:21:22,162
That is the burden we all carry.

371
00:21:22,820 --> 00:21:24,280
Can you say the same?

372
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:28,000
Because I'm raring to go. What?

373
00:21:28,960 --> 00:21:29,790
What?

374
00:21:29,873 --> 00:21:30,777
You can't mean...

375
00:21:30,860 --> 00:21:31,877
You're crazy!

376
00:21:31,960 --> 00:21:32,860
There's no way!

377
00:21:33,060 --> 00:21:35,472
Both of my goals are really quite doable.

378
00:21:35,640 --> 00:21:38,816
As long as I get you off
this speeding train, that is.

379
00:21:39,120 --> 00:21:42,837
Killing you will break the aging
spell, thereby reviving my crew.

380
00:21:42,920 --> 00:21:44,377
Trish isn't going anywhere!

381
00:21:44,460 --> 00:21:45,660
You're a damn fool!

382
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:47,842
If you want to die, do it alone!

383
00:21:48,120 --> 00:21:50,220
We're going over 150 an hour!

384
00:21:50,460 --> 00:21:51,500
Ironic, isn't it?

385
00:21:51,640 --> 00:21:54,464
You're the one who grabbed
me, if you'll recall.

386
00:21:59,080 --> 00:21:59,910
No!

387
00:21:59,993 --> 00:22:01,597
I refuse to die like this!

388
00:22:01,680 --> 00:22:02,860
It's Jacksonville!

389
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:34,840
I don't give a damn about nothing else.

390
00:22:35,140 --> 00:22:38,377
Freaking you is all I need.

391
00:22:38,460 --> 00:22:43,020
I need your body.

392
00:22:44,860 --> 00:22:47,957
I want you to make out my time.

393
00:22:48,040 --> 00:22:50,017
I want you to make it.

394
00:22:50,100 --> 00:22:55,317
I want you to make out my time.

395
00:22:55,400 --> 00:22:57,020
Hey, yeah, yeah, yeah.

396
00:23:08,040 --> 00:23:10,840
Tell me.

397
00:23:27,740 --> 00:23:30,717
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

398
00:23:30,800 --> 00:23:32,240
Oh, yeah, oh, yeah.

399
00:23:32,880 --> 00:23:34,000
I'm freaking.

400
00:23:57,460 --> 00:23:58,820
Thank you.
